                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8fd5f9f-14bf-3829-96ee-988f5c01c903",
                                        "entry_id": "660cefb7-4b12-375d-b017-03910294bbb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in an efficacious manner"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7db3a94f-3d37-4745-bee3-a9abbcf54c92",
                        "source_entry_id": "547d476f-2e24-389b-bbfc-db2fe6d3a843",
                        "source_sense_id": "066c4976-b74d-32c8-95bc-48326bd3bfc5",
                        "target_lang_word": "effectively",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "effectively",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0ee9aa0a-0439-30e1-9b34-627b0d0e9113",
                                        "entry_id": "46cce09a-e0d3-3b71-b409-f04006fcaf0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an efficient or effective manner; with powerful effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c27c348f-5b80-45c6-9c7f-76b69e706e9d",
                                                "sense_id": "0ee9aa0a-0439-30e1-9b34-627b0d0e9113",
                                                "text": "The nightclubs generally provide liquor (at a price), pretty girls who are clad diaphanously but extremely effectively, a tiny space in which to dance [...] and food[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "656420f4-c490-4315-bdb9-9db5d57f37cc",
                                                "sense_id": "0ee9aa0a-0439-30e1-9b34-627b0d0e9113",
                                                "text": "A state ideology, mixing nationalism, and basic Marxist economics, going under the name \"Juche\", was constructed, and Kim Il-sung effectively silenced, disposed of and cleared away any opposition, isolating the country and exercising an iron grip on the military, the state media and the government and party organs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c769a58-c3d9-36b1-b190-dcc9fb2a67bd",
                                        "entry_id": "46cce09a-e0d3-3b71-b409-f04006fcaf0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Essentially, in effect, for all practical purposes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81ae00b7-ecd6-4069-b28b-3e6bebcb1894",
                                                "sense_id": "8c769a58-c3d9-36b1-b190-dcc9fb2a67bd",
                                                "text": "On paper, the answer seems to be yes, but, effectively, the answer is no."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61c746af-2871-4292-8ff3-c23dcf5d52b4",
                                                "sense_id": "8c769a58-c3d9-36b1-b190-dcc9fb2a67bd",
                                                "text": "A doorknob of whatever roundish shape is effectively a continuum of levers, with the axis of the latching mechanism—known as the spindle—being the fulcrum about which the turning takes place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4ac177e1-a3db-4bc6-888b-3369a9704e08",
                        "source_entry_id": "547d476f-2e24-389b-bbfc-db2fe6d3a843",
                        "source_sense_id": "066c4976-b74d-32c8-95bc-48326bd3bfc5",
                        "target_lang_word": "efficiently",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "efficiently",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2b1ef4a-3b6e-3b44-bdbb-4a8a9bfc5239",
                                        "entry_id": "7c23fb0f-53cc-39c7-8cfe-e3729c188065",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an efficient manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d622fd70-34a4-4a24-a8ae-12e4bad4192d",
                                                "sense_id": "b2b1ef4a-3b6e-3b44-bdbb-4a8a9bfc5239",
                                                "text": "The second half was a less open affair, in which West Brom grew increasingly and efficiently conservative."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d381d9aa-5458-45e5-8100-0c38978e7a56",
                        "source_entry_id": "547d476f-2e24-389b-bbfc-db2fe6d3a843",
                        "source_sense_id": "066c4976-b74d-32c8-95bc-48326bd3bfc5",
                        "target_lang_word": "effectually",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "effectually",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6a92ace-0afe-3658-95d0-804d288d346a",
                                        "entry_id": "2036caf8-12b3-3742-8f0c-c24e3a61d45d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In such a way as to achieve a desired result; effectively; so as to have an effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a17299f0-4674-468c-9568-bd393147fc1c",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a92ace-0afe-3658-95d0-804d288d346a",
                                                "text": "Though the captain had effectually demolished poor Partridge, yet had he not reaped the harvest he hoped for, which was to turn the foundling out of Mr Allworthy's house."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e920d167-44c6-40cd-b9f5-38cbedf5faa8",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a92ace-0afe-3658-95d0-804d288d346a",
                                                "text": "Her quick eye detected the cause in a moment; Mr. Courtenaye had just entered the room, though he had not as yet perceived them. Indeed, the position in which Ethel stood effectually screened her from observation; and Henrietta thought she could not do better than stand as they were, thus giving her companion time to recover her outward composure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1233bfd-6ea0-47dd-aea4-03281e4d35a1",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a92ace-0afe-3658-95d0-804d288d346a",
                                                "text": "They intrigued and slandered and hated each other only on that account, - but as to effectually lifting a little finger - oh, no."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
